+# The binary's admission test rejects, once `--warmup` records have been seen, any sequence
+# whose count of never-seen k-mers exceeds mean + 5 SD of the running counts. Upstream built it
+# to drop error-laden genome assemblies. On a gene cohort the first record contributes every
+# k-mer and the rest almost none, so SD ~ L/sqrt(n) and a genuinely new lineage arriving late
+# is rejected, together with every later member of it (a rejected record never enters the
+# count-min sketch). Walker and LexicMap rows have already been checked, so admission is off:
+# a warmup the run can never reach (the binary parses it with atoi, so INT_MAX).
+ADMISSION_OFF_WARMUP = 2**31 - 1
